
# <KEY>: <Summary as a capitalized, imperative sentence.>
#
# <Body: why the change was needed and what it does now.>
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Follows the Apache Guacamole commit conventions, adapted for molcajete.
#
# Subject line
#   <KEY>: <Summary>.
#   - KEY is the GitHub issue the change belongs to, written as GH-<n>
#     (do not use "#<n>": git strips lines that start with "#").
#     With no issue, use the component instead: gateway, client, daemon,
#     protocol, telemetry, web, deploy, docker, docs.
#   - Summary starts with a capital letter, uses the imperative mood
#     ("Add", "Fix", "Handle", not "Added" / "Fixes"), and ends with a
#     period. Keep it within about 72 characters.
#   - Every commit for one issue uses the same KEY, so the history of an
#     issue reads as a series: GH-12: Add ..., GH-12: Address review
#     feedback on ...
#   - Merge commits: <KEY>: Merge <summary in lowercase>.
#       GH-12: Merge serial console protocol support.
#
# Body (optional for trivial changes, separated by one blank line)
#   - Wrap at 72 characters.
#   - Describe the problem first: what happened, under which conditions,
#     and why. Then describe the behavior after the change ("The terminal
#     is now kept at least one character in each dimension...").
#   - Mention related issues by KEY ("GH-7 removed ..., so ...").
#   - For several independent changes, use "- " bullets and indent
#     continuation lines by two spaces. Group them under short headings
#     ending in ":" when there are many.
#   - Mention small side fixes at the end ("Also fixes ...").
#
# Examples
#   GH-12: Handle terminal dimensions with no valid copy or draw range.
#
#   A viewport smaller than one character produced a terminal with zero
#   rows or columns, after which redraws requested empty column ranges
#   and hit the assertion in fit_to_range(), aborting the connection.
#
#   The terminal is now kept at least one character in each dimension,
#   and copy and set operations ignore requests with no valid range.
#
#   gateway: Log X-Real-IP before X-Forwarded-For.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
